WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
A doctor injects a patient
with something radioactive.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.690
On purpose.

3
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.850
It lets the doctor see inside
the body without a single cut.

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.850
A few days later, almost none
of that radioactivity is left.

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.230
Nobody took it out.

6
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.170
So where did it go?

7
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.270
In this mission, you'll see
why nobody can predict when a

8
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.110
single nucleus will decay,

9
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.390
and how half-life lets you
predict a whole sample anyway.

10
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.870
You'll meet the background
radiation that is around us all the

11
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.210
time, and match each kind of
radiation to the job it does best.

12
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.930
Your mission: find out where
the radioactivity went.
